.TH AMP-TRIM 1 "November 2026" "animated-pager" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
amp-trim \- clean and bound a script(1) typescript for an animated man-page box
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B amp-trim
.BR \-t " timing"
.BR \-s " typescript"
.RI [ options ]
.P
.B amp-trim
.BR \-t " timing"
.BR \-s " typescript"
.BR \-W " width"
.BR \-H " height"
.RB [ \-S " shift]"
.BR \-T " out-timing"
.BR \-O " out-typescript"
.RB [ \-v ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B amp-trim
reads a timing file and the corresponding typescript produced by
.BR script (1)
and prepares them for use inside a fixed-size animation region
(for example the box managed by
.BR animated_pager ).
.P
Two modes of operation are supported:
.TP
.B Detection mode
When
.B \-\-width
and
.B \-\-height
are both omitted the tool only measures the content.
It strips the same dangerous control sequences that would be removed in
trim mode, then prints the minimal bounding box (width and height) that
would contain every remaining character.
The two numbers are written to standard output (so they can be captured by
a script) and a human-readable summary is written to standard error.
No output files are required.
.TP
.B Trim mode
When both
.B \-\-width
and
.B \-\-height
are supplied the tool produces a new timing/typescript pair whose visible
content is constrained to that rectangle.
.SS Cleaning
The following sequences are removed because they would fight the
surrounding pager:
.IP \(bu 2
CSI sequences that clear the screen or home the cursor
.RI ( J ", " H ", " K ", mode setters, \.\.\.)
.IP \(bu 2
ESC c / ESC C (full reset)
.IP \(bu 2
Relative cursor-movement sequences that could leave the box
.IP \(bu 2
Form-feed characters
.P
Colour / SGR sequences
.RI ( \e033[ \.\.\. m )
are preserved so that caca-style and other coloured frames continue to work.
.SS Horizontal handling
.IP \(bu 2
.B Shift
.RB ( \-S / \-\-shift N )
discards the first
.I N
columns of every line.
Timing that belonged to those characters is retained.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Width
truncates each line to the requested number of columns.
Again the timing of the discarded characters is kept.
.SS Vertical handling
A sliding window of the last
.I height
lines is maintained.
When a new line would exceed the window the oldest line is dropped and the
remaining lines move up – exactly the behaviour of a terminal whose height
is equal to the requested value.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timing " " \fIfile\fR
Input timing file (required).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-typescript " " \fIfile\fR
Input typescript file (required).
.TP
.BR \-W ", " \-\-width " " \fIn\fR
Target width in columns.
Must be supplied together with
.B \-\-height
(or both must be omitted for detection mode).
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-height " " \fIn\fR
Target height in rows.
Must be supplied together with
.B \-\-width
(or both must be omitted for detection mode).
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-shift " " \fIn\fR
Shift the visible window to the right by
.I n
columns (default 0).
Timing for the skipped columns is retained.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-out\-timing " " \fIfile\fR
Output timing file.
Required in trim mode; ignored in detection mode.
.TP
.BR \-O ", " \-\-out\-typescript " " \fIfile\fR
Output typescript file.
Required in trim mode; ignored in detection mode.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print a detailed report of every class of character or escape sequence that
was removed, shifted or truncated.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
No usable events could be parsed from the input files.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error or a required input file is missing / unreadable.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Detect the natural size of a recording
.EX
amp-trim -t session.tm -s session.ts
.EE
.P
Typical output on stdout:
.EX
72 24
.EE
.SS Trim to a 40×8 box, discarding the first two columns
.EX
amp-trim -t session.tm -s session.ts \\
         -W 40 -H 8 -S 2 \\
         -T box.tm -O box.ts
.EE
.SS Obtain statistics about what was removed
.EX
amp-trim -t session.tm -s session.ts -W 40 -H 8 \\
         -T box.tm -O box.ts --verbose
.EE
.SH NOTES
For best visual results record the original typescript in a terminal whose
size is close to the final animation box, or run the recording through
.B amp-trim
before feeding it to the pager.
.P
Because timing of truncated or shifted characters is deliberately retained,
the overall duration of the replay stays the same even when many characters
are discarded.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR script (1),
.BR scriptreplay (1),
.BR animated_pager (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Animated-pager demo
